  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Jerk",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "jerk"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " seasoning is built around allspice and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "scotch bonnet",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "scotch-bonnet"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " chillies. The scotch bonnet brings both heat and a fruity sweetness that no other chilli replicates. Allspice, thyme, garlic and ginger complete the paste. The marinade penetrates the chicken over a long overnight rest, seasoning it all the way to the bone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use bone-in, skin-on thighs for the best results. The skin chars and crisps on the griddle while the bone helps the meat cook evenly and stay moist. Rest the chicken for 5 minutes after grilling before serving."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
